Error [E0140]: `workers` still owes `consume`
  --> task_list_drain_that_reinserts_still_owes_consume.jet:3:5
    |
  3 |     workers := [Task<Int>]{}
    |     ^^^^^^^
 Why: This value's type is `#SingleUse`, so it carries a job that has to be done — dropping it without doing that job leaves the work undone (an unjoined task, an unreleased lock)
 Fix: Consume it exactly once: move it to a parameter with the move marker `^`, or `return` it — or write `#Unsafe("reason") { consume(workers) }` to discard it deliberately
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0140
